The least common multiple of 3, 4, 6, and 7 is 84.

There will be 84 school days from today when they all work together tutoring in the lab.

In how many days from the current day will Darren work the sixth time?
Note:
Since in this problem both Darren and Chi have different schedule patterns, this task should not be done with the same number of days. Therefore, we have to find the LCM of 4, 6, and 7, to know how many times Darren works in 4 days, 6 days, and 7 days:

$\text{(6, 4) = 4, (4, 4) = 4}$;
$\text{(6, 6) =6, (4,6) =6} $;
$\text{(6,7) = 42, (6,7) = 42} $;
L.C.M$(4,6,7) = 84$.
